## Uncore

### Mid-level cache

# Enable use of a midlevel cache between i/d and L1
# 2 MiB (2097152 bytes) = 2048 sets x 16 ways x 64 B
--mlc_present                   1
--mlc_size                      2097152
--mlc_assoc                     16
--mlc_cycles                    11  # L2 load-use 16 = AGEN(1) + dcache 4 + 11


### LLC
# 3.75 MiB (3932160 bytes) = 4096 sets x 15 ways x 64 B: golden_small's LLC with twice the
# sets. Latency is left at golden_small's value.
--l1_size                       3932160
--l1_banks                      8
--l1_cycles		                66          # L3 load-use 86 = L2 16 + 4 transfer/fill + 66
--l1_assoc                      15
--l1_line_size                  64
--l1_interleave_factor          64

### Cache hierarchy policy
# Unlike golden_small, the L1 (LLC) is not exclusive: a miss fills the line into every
# level, so the LLC normally also holds what L2 holds (the pre-Skylake-SP arrangement,
# which is why the LLC is doubled). This is not strictly inclusive: Scarab has no
# back-invalidation, so an LLC eviction leaves any L2/L1 copy in place and there are
# no inclusion victims.
--exclusive_l1                  0


